# CEDAR backend - database configuration
#
# DATABASE_URL is REQUIRED. The application (backend and Alembic) will
# refuse to start if it is not set - there is no hardcoded fallback,
# because the correct value differs between the two supported ways of
# running CEDAR locally:
#
# 1) Full Docker (backend AND PostgreSQL both run as containers via
#    `docker compose up --build`):
#    docker-compose.yml already injects DATABASE_URL automatically for
#    the backend container. You do NOT need this file for that scenario.
#    The value used internally is:
#      DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://cedar:cedar@db:5432/cedar
#
# 2) Hybrid development (PostgreSQL runs in Docker, backend runs locally
#    via venv/uvicorn):
#    docker-compose.yml maps the container's internal port 5432 to port
#    5433 on your host machine ("5433:5432"). From your local machine,
#    "localhost"/"127.0.0.1" is your own host, not the Docker network, so
#    you must connect through the published host port (5433), not the
#    internal container port (5432).
#
#    NOTE: this .env file is NOT loaded automatically by the app. Copy
#    this file to backend/.env for reference, but you must still export
#    DATABASE_URL in your shell before running uvicorn or alembic
#    locally, e.g. (PowerShell):
#      $env:DATABASE_URL="postgresql+psycopg2://cedar:cedar@127.0.0.1:5433/cedar"

DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://cedar:cedar@127.0.0.1:5433/cedar